## Fonts

Load from Google Fonts with `preconnect`. Request the **latin, latin-ext, cyrillic and cyrillic-ext** subsets (the browser fetches only what a page needs). Mongolian needs Ө, ө, Ү, ү, which live in the cyrillic-ext subset, so it must be present.

| Family | Weights | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| Inter Tight (variable) | 100 to 900 | All labels, nav, titles, years, buttons, footer text, the giant background letters (800) |
| Newsreader (variable, roman + italic) | 400 | Latin text of the synopsis and the italic credit |
| Source Serif 4 (roman + italic) | 400 | Cyrillic glyphs of the synopsis and credit. It is second in the serif stack, so it is used automatically wherever Newsreader has no glyph |

- Remove Noto Sans JP, Noto Serif SC, "Noto Sans JP Big", Poppins and Cormorant Garamond. There is no Japanese or Chinese text any more, and Poppins has no Cyrillic. In the footer, Poppins becomes Inter Tight (same weights, same sizes); the Cormorant wordmark becomes the mlibrary wordmark in Inter Tight 600.
- `<html lang>` follows the active language (`mn` or `en`). Use `hyphens: auto` and `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on running text only, never on single-line labels.

