## Routes

| Route | Page | Footer |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | Curved archive hero (Appendix B) | its own small footer line |
| `/books` | Flat shelf hero (Appendix A) | its own small footer line |
| `/books/:id` | Flat shelf with that book's detail sheet open | same |
| `/about`, `/journal`, `/journal/:slug`, `/contact`, `/legal/:slug` | Normal scrolling pages in the paper style | **big footer** (Appendix C) |
| `*` | Not found | big footer |

- On `/`, opening a book adds `?book=<id>` to the URL; on `/books` it navigates to `/books/:id`. Closing the sheet or pressing the browser Back button closes it. Opening a deep link snaps the shelf to that book and shows the sheet immediately (use the reduced-motion durations for that first open).
- The flat shelf reads `?decade=1970` and selects that decade tab on load.
- Route changes use a paper sheet (`--sheet`) that grows over the screen with `clip-path` (about 600 ms, `cubic-bezier(.76,0,.18,1)`) and then retreats. No opacity fades. With `prefers-reduced-motion` the swap is instant.
- The flat shelf and the curved archive show the **same data**, so every field of the detail sheet is identical in both.

## Shared header (replaces both hero top bars)

Use the visual design of Appendix B's top bar (76px, 36px padding, all cobalt). The flat shelf's own "BACK / logo / CAREER" bar is removed; both heroes sit under this header.

- **Left:** the `mlibrary` lockup, a link to `/`.
- **Right:** `BOOKS`, `ABOUT`, `JOURNAL` (EN) or `НОМ`, `ТУХАЙ`, `ТЭМДЭГЛЭЛ` (MN), then the **language toggle**, then the burger.
- **Language toggle:** a boxed control (21px tall, 1px cobalt border) with two buttons `EN` and `MN` in a role="group" labelled "Language". The active one has a cobalt fill with white text; the fill slides between the two with the same `.6s var(--ease)` motion as the decade tab indicator. Each button has `aria-pressed`. On phones it stays visible next to the burger.
- **Burger** (two 1.5px lines, 26 × 12px) opens the **menu sheet**: a full-screen paper sheet that grows out of the burger with the same clip-path motion as the detail sheet. Inside: the four links (Books, About, Journal, Contact) in Inter Tight 600, `clamp(44px, 8vw, 96px)`, cobalt, each revealed by a mask slide with 75 ms stagger; the language toggle; the email and the "FB / IG" links. A boxed Close button sits where the burger was. Escape closes it. Focus moves into the sheet and returns to the burger on close.
- The active route's link has a 1px cobalt underline.

## Language switching (EN / MN)

- Default language is **Mongolian**. Remember the choice in `localStorage` (inside try/catch) and honour `?lang=en|mn`. Update `<html lang>` and `document.title` on every switch.
- Switching is instant and **does not reload, reset the route or move the shelf**. Engines expose `setLocale(strings)`: they rewrite only text nodes, labels and `aria-label`s. In the heroes the caption swaps with the normal mask slide (`dir = +1`); everywhere else the text is replaced in place. No opacity fade anywhere in the heroes.
- All visible text comes from `src/i18n/en.js` and `src/i18n/mn.js`, which must have exactly the same keys. Add `npm run check:i18n`, a small script that fails when the key sets differ or a Mongolian value contains no Cyrillic letter. Missing keys fall back to English.
- Book titles on the covers stay as drawn. The caption title, detail title, synopsis, genre, labels and every other HTML text follow the active language.

## Mongolian must never break the layout (most important rule)

Mongolian strings are usually 20 to 40 percent longer than English and use Ө ө Ү ү. For every text element:

- No fixed widths on text. Use `min-width: 0`, `max-width` and `clamp()`. Single-line labels get `white-space: nowrap`; running text may wrap.
- Decade tabs, language toggle, nav links and footer links must still fit at 320px wide (reduce padding with `clamp`, hide the nav text below 768px as Appendix B does).
- Caption title: `text-wrap: balance`, and the title mask must allow two lines on phones without clipping descenders.
- Footer columns use `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on headings and links; the 5-column grid never causes horizontal scroll.
- The giant background letters use Cyrillic (see below), not CJK, and must stay behind the shelf and never overlap the caption at any width.
- Verify, in **both languages**, at 320, 360, 390, 414, 600, 768, 820, 1024, 1280, 1440 and 1920 px: no horizontal scroll, no clipped or overlapping text, no label wrapping onto two lines, the tabs, arrows, caption, timeline and footer lines never collide. Fix the cause in CSS, not by shrinking fonts below the sizes in the appendices.

